@@ -47,6 +47,11 @@ You can find our backwards-compatibility policy [here](https://github.com/hynek/
 
   [#675](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/675)
 
+- `structlog.processors.ExceptionRenderer` (and therefore `structlog.processors.format_exc_info` and `structlog.processors.dict_tracebacks`) doesn't add an `exception` key anymore if there is no exception – for example, when calling `exception()` outside of an exception handler.
+  Custom exception formatters are therefore not called with `(None, None, None)` anymore.
+
+  [#676](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/676)
+
 
